-- title:
--   Closed cubes are closed sets
-- statement:
--   For $h \ge 0$ and $u \in \mathbb{R}^d$, the closed cube
--   $$\overline{A}_h(u) \;=\; \bigl\{x \in \mathbb{R}^d : \|x-u\|_\infty \le \tfrac h2\bigr\},
--   \qquad \|x\|_\infty = \sup_i |x_i|,$$
--   of centre $u$ and side length $h$ is a closed subset of $\mathbb{R}^d$.
--
--   Closedness is what makes these cubes compact (they are also bounded), which is the property used whenever a covering, a finiteness or a Vitali-type argument is run on the family of cubes; it also gives measurability for free.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The ambient space is `EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d)` with its Euclidean topology, while the cube is defined by the maximum norm; the two norms are equivalent, and the statement is about the Euclidean topology.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/dbenbenn/quadratic-forms-sobolev/blob/7a1a680db2124d46ce370c91fd450aa454edf491/QuadraticFormsSobolev/LebesgueDiff.lean#L52-L55

